<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shaftesbury</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shaftesbury is a hilltop town in north <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dorset">Dorset</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. Founded as a fortified burh by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great">Alfred the Great</a> around 880, it grew around the wealthy nunnery of Shaftesbury Abbey, which Alfred established with his daughter Æthelgifu as abbess. King Edward the Martyr was buried in the abbey, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cnut-the-great">Cnut the Great</a> died at Shaftesbury in 1035. The abbey was dissolved in 1539.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shaftesbury.jpg" alt="Shaftesbury" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Robin Drayton · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:High_Street,_Shaftesbury_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1440129.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
